        "topic": "Metal extraction methods",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2001",
        "question_text": "<p>The process of extracting iron from its ore using a blast furnace involves the reduction of <b>haematite</b> ($Fe_2O_3$) with which of the following?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>In a blast furnace, haematite ($Fe_2O_3$) is reduced to iron by carbon monoxide (CO), which is produced from the reaction of coke (carbon) with oxygen. The chemical equation for the reduction is: $Fe_2O_3 + 3CO \rightarrow 2Fe + 3CO_2$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "75623",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "Hydrogen gas ($H_2$)",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "75624",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "Carbon monoxide (CO)",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "75625",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "Nitrogen gas ($N_2$)",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "75626",
                "tag": "d",
                "text": "Oxygen gas ($O_2$)",
                "is_correct": false
            }
        ],
        "_page_num": 1,
